<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#jong-ship">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jong (ship)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The jong was a large ocean-going ship of the Javanese and Malay world, capable of carrying large crews and cargoes. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a>'s naval forces used such ships to transport troops, horses and supplies across the archipelago. They were crucial to the Majapahit Empire's control over its maritime territories.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jong-ship.jpg" alt="Jong (ship)" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hieronymus Megiser (translator), Ludovico di Varthema (original work) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Situs_civitatis_Bantam_et_Navium_Insulae_Iauae_delineatio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
